      "writtenOn": "2022-08-31T12:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rationale for current time millis is better:\n1. We don\u0027t really have a thing that is really rely on monotonic clock.\n2. The ctm-based timestamp might differ from the timstamp we see in the device log.  Which might make it harder to debug and clarify issue since they might not match if the user adjust system time multiple times.\n3. The use cases described were not a problem happened in pratice when we debug other modules. If it happens, we ask for clarifying the time change or just let the reporter reproduce again without touching the time.\n4. The conversion between a ctm-base timestamp and a real timestamp got from ctm is unknown to me. And I think people would be confused too.",
      "parentUuid": "bf4f3aa0_f960b2e0",
      "range": {
